# Commits normalise to LF; a Windows checkout gets CRLF back. The corpus was
# measured on the CRLF working copies and re-measured on an LF checkout before
# this file was settled on — the numbers are in EVIDENCE.md and both forms pass.
#
# *.gz is marked binary because those fixtures are gzip payloads whose bytes are
# the thing under test. The other byte-sensitive fixtures (latin1.xml, the
# deliberately-truncated files) git already classifies as binary on its own;
# verified with `git check-attr` and a full checkout round-trip rather than
# assumed from reading this.
* text=auto
*.gz binary
